WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.073
The flow works on the Cholesky factorization.

00:00:03.153 --> 00:00:06.717
Any positive-definite matrix is L times L-transpose,

00:00:06.797 --> 00:00:12.673
so a d-dimensional precision matrix needs only d
times d plus one, over two, numbers.

00:00:12.753 --> 00:00:16.947
The flow pushes a base vector through
Sum-of-Sigmoids layers,

00:00:17.027 --> 00:00:22.763
reshapes it into a triangular matrix, forces the
diagonal positive with a softplus,

00:00:22.843 --> 00:00:24.935
and takes the Cholesky product,

00:00:25.015 --> 00:00:29.489
so every output is a valid precision matrix with
cheap Jacobians.

00:00:29.569 --> 00:00:32.082
A hypernetwork feeds in lambda and q,

00:00:32.162 --> 00:00:39.369
and training minimizes the KL divergence to the
unnormalized posterior under a generalized-Normal prior.

00:00:39.449 --> 00:00:43.083
Lasso appears at q equals one, Ridge at q equals two,

00:00:43.163 --> 00:00:46.096
and smaller q reaches the sub-l-one regime.
